r": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01FGZcx36oqPFLJj4sPECjbC", "tool": "wait_for_ci", "args": {"run_id": "ci-0002"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 742054, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01FGZcx36oqPFLJj4sPECjbC", "tool": "wait_for_ci", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 742054, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01FGZcx36oqPFLJj4sPECjbC", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 745820, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0144iC1479P8DEwrKYGeTjfT", "tool": "open_pr", "args": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "`src/money.py`'s `round_money` documented banker's rounding (FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, causing `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build (e.g. 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66).\n\nThis switches the quantize rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0002 passed on 0a9452f727 (branch updated with latest main).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 746720, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0144iC1479P8DEwrKYGeTjfT", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 746720, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0144iC1479P8DEwrKYGeTjfT", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 751447, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** in `src/money.py`, `round_money` claimed to use banker's rounding (FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. That's why 2.665 came out as 2.67 instead of the 2.66 the test expects.\n- **The fix:** I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`.\n- **CI:** it passed on my commit. When I first tried to open the PR, it was rejected because the branch was behind main. I merged the latest main into the branch, re-ran CI on the updated branch, and it passed again before I opened the PR.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI didn't merge it, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval. Also, I couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory tool doesn't recognise it. The change follows what the code comment and the test say FIN-212 requires.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PBbFeqxNgJpQMkULkQEaRQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NreZKmW8X4vbgVAGcZwBxW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01RrRYDfecoZVLpvaXwWQP98", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01UV6W8hLQEkV21ikfzVJKyN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Uajvn7ZT5zAunbcCjD2rGf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AAPuzt1GX2Q4i2cJjqQA7d", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014nnkGpN4qgFNNuu4gLAErP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014JudxWAz9R768LFrGC8DKr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "`src/money.py`'s `round_money` documented banker's rounding (FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, causing `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build (e.g. 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66).\n\nThis switches the quantize rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_011btKLYxcY7xnGWAWpc7w5n", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "update_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The branch now includes new commits from main, so I'll re-run CI on the updated head before opening the PR.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01D6S8eP